commit 00ce692c7f6ea1900888a2a24aecf6cba5544ae1
Author: Peter Hutterer <peter.hutterer@who-t.net>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 17:04:35 2026 +1000

    randr: fix size and offset in RRChangeProviderProperty PrependMode
    
    RRChangeProviderProperty() has two bugs in the PropModePrepend case:
    
    1. new_value.size is set to 'len' (the new data length) instead of
       'total_len' (len + prop_value->size), losing track of the existing
       data. This also affects PropModeAppend.
    
    2. The old_data offset is computed using prop_value->size instead of
       len. For PrependMode, the layout should be [new(len)][old(size)],
       so old_data should start at len * size_in_bytes.
    
    These bugs are analogous to the ones fixed in RRChangeOutputProperty(),
    see commit 541ab2ecd41d ("Xi/randr: fix handling of PropModeAppend/Prepend").
    
    This vulnerability was discovered by:
      Anonymous working with TrendAI Zero Day Initiative
    
    ZDI-CAN-31944
    
